# Intent: "Use this network now" for a real away test without carrying the unit out of range of the home Wi-Fi (owner 2026-11-14): self.wifi.use_now(index) sets the station to the chosen saved network and drops the old link, so the Wi-Fi component reconnects to the chosen one (a plain disconnect made it rejoin the old network, 2026-11-14). The join is bounded to 15 s: a network not found, a refused password or no address sends the unit back to the previous network at once with a plain reason (events wifi_use_step, wifi_use_revert); after an address, the hub must be reached within 3 minutes (wifi_use_ok) or the unit goes back. The saved list in flash and in memory is never edited. The three tools that add, forget or switch saved networks end a watch first.
# Check after a flash: self.wifi.use_now(index of a network in range) answers {"ok":true,"revert_in_s":180,"join_limit_s":15}; the log shows steps switching, leaving_current_network, got_ip, hub_reached; a network out of range reverts within about 10 s with wifi_use_revert network_not_found; self.wifi.list_saved lists every network afterwards.
